{
  "name": "Getting a Smooth Door Frame Installation",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Installing a door frame might seem straightforward, but there are a few key steps to make sure it's done right and functions perfectly. First off, you've gotta measure that opening super carefully. Once you've got your frame, check for plumb, square, and level conditions – this is crucial! An out-of-whack frame means a door that won't close properly or will constantly bind. Next, correct the hinge and strike alignment. This often involves some shimming or adjusting the jamb before you even think about reattaching the trim and hardware. You might find yourself needing to trim the door slab or adjust the hinges a few times to get everything just right. It's a process that sometimes involves iterative adjustments, not just a simple swap, especially if there's existing damage or misalignment. Don't rush this part, take your time, and don't be afraid to bring in an expert if things get tricky. Getting it perfect upfront saves a ton of headaches down the road.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
